# 6. Values sent back to the slide

The control points of a curve, dragged with the mouse: a Bezier curve, which approaches its points, or a
Catmull-Rom spline, which goes through them. The program computes the length of the curve, and the slide shows
it while you drag: a value that goes from the demo to the slide.

